e": "", "id": 1, "text": "<strong>John: </strong>  Sure! The test should be a little bit difficult. We'd better review the topics. <br>"}, {"time": "9300", "image": "", "id": 2, "text": "<strong>Lyanna: </strong>  Well, public cloud providers allow users to move data, even entire Virtual Machines may be uploaded. This narrows the possibilities of moving whole data. <br>"}, {"time": "20000", "image": "", "id": 3, "text": "<strong>John: </strong>  Right, but there are cloud providers that have been offering services where VMs can be transferred. <br>"}, {"time": "26000", "image": "", "id": 4, "text": "<strong>Lyanna: </strong>  True. And in case the user is not able to upload the VM, the file level migration works well most of the times. Some appliances also allow you to move and replicate data in local storage. <br>"}, {"time": "38000", "image": "", "id": 5, "text": "<strong>John: </strong>  And that's advantageous because it improves the way people manage information. Don't forget that blocks of data can also be transferred or migrated. <br>"}, {"time": "46200", "image": "", "id": 6, "text": "<strong>Lyanna: </strong>  Thanks for reminding me that. Now, let's move to the elements that can be backed up, shall we? <br>"}, {"time": "51500", "image": "", "id": 7, "text": "<strong>John: </strong>  Ok. First, it is important to back up files. Having up-to-date data is always important and very practical. I've been continuously updating my info for two years. How about you? <br>"}, {"time": "64500", "image": "", "id": 8, "text": "<strong>Lyanna: </strong>  So, have I. A life saver! Once, my laptop crashed and I lost my final project; luckily, I had backed up my documents two days before. But let's continue with the elements. <br>"}, {"time": "76300", "image": "", "id": 9, "text": "<strong>John: </strong>  Alright. Among the most important are documents, application data, and system. People have experienced the loss of such documents and they can't be easily restored. Once it's gone, it's gone forever. <br>"}, {"time": "90000", "image": "", "id": 10, "text": "<strong>Lyanna: </strong>  True. But there are others like media, heirlooms, and even back up. Never trust only one back up system. Always play safe and have different resources from where you can get your files back. Though technology should be evolving continuously, it's better to prepare for disaster. <br>"}]}, "type": "video"}], "type": "video", "_data": [], "id": 3, "title": ""}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "id": 0}]}